WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:06.045
In this video, you will put your own house on the map, so families can find your lights and drive by.

00:00:06.045 --> 00:00:08.978
You will add the address, a description, and photos.

00:00:08.978 --> 00:00:10.085
We start on the map.

00:00:10.987 --> 00:00:15.049
To begin, open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:15.049 --> 00:00:17.174
That is the only address you need.

00:00:20.036 --> 00:00:22.443
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:22.443 --> 00:00:26.187
The first time you visit, it asks to use your location.

00:00:26.187 --> 00:00:27.524
Tap Use my location.

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:33.999
That is how the map shows how far things are, and gives you directions.

00:00:33.999 --> 00:00:37.204
Your browser asks permission as well, so tap Allow.

00:00:37.204 --> 00:00:41.765
Your location is used only on your device, and you can say no at any time.

00:00:45.429 --> 00:00:48.118
Now look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:48.118 --> 00:00:49.313
See the three dots?

00:00:49.313 --> 00:00:53.616
That is the menu, and it is the doorway to everything else on the site.

00:00:53.616 --> 00:00:54.154
Tap them.

00:00:57.274 --> 00:00:58.537
In the menu, tap Add.

00:00:58.537 --> 00:01:02.842
That is where you add anything new: an event, a contest, or your own house.

00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:06.274
Now tap A lighting display.

00:01:06.274 --> 00:01:13.315
This is for showing off your own house, or a house you decorated for a customer, so families can drive by and see it.

00:01:15.222 --> 00:01:16.194
Who is posting?

00:01:16.194 --> 00:01:18.322
A homeowner is for your own house.

00:01:18.322 --> 00:01:21.847
A professional installer is for a house your company did.

00:01:21.847 --> 00:01:24.886
We are a homeowner, so tap A homeowner, then Next.

00:01:27.513 --> 00:01:28.900
Type the name to show.

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:33.243
This is the name people see on the map, for example, the Garcia family.

00:01:33.243 --> 00:01:35.535
It does not have to be your full name.

00:01:37.324 --> 00:01:39.349
Did a company install your lights?

00:01:39.349 --> 00:01:43.514
If one did, you can name them, and your display links to their profile.

00:01:43.514 --> 00:01:45.943
We did it ourselves, so tap No, then Next.

00:01:48.626 --> 00:01:50.636
Which season is this display for?

00:01:50.636 --> 00:01:55.127
Visitors pick a season on the map, so choose the one your lights belong to.

00:01:55.127 --> 00:01:56.605
Tap Christmas, then Next.

00:01:59.292 --> 00:02:02.747
Give the display a name, and tell us what makes it special.

00:02:02.747 --> 00:02:05.857
Is it the music, the animation, the number of lights?

00:02:05.857 --> 00:02:09.254
Families read this to decide whether it is worth the drive.

00:02:13.121 --> 00:02:14.128
Add the address.

00:02:14.128 --> 00:02:21.121
This is where the pin goes, and visitors see it so they can drive by, so only add an address you want people to visit.

00:02:24.252 --> 00:02:30.517
Tell families when the lights are on, and how to enjoy them, like drive by, walk by, or where to park.

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:34.470
Good directions make for happier visitors, and happier neighbors.

00:02:36.447 --> 00:02:37.158
Add photos.

00:02:37.158 --> 00:02:39.527
Take them at night, with the lights on.

00:02:39.527 --> 00:02:42.548
The first photo is the cover people see on the map.

00:02:45.601 --> 00:02:48.904
Finally, check everything, and tap Put it on the map.

00:02:48.904 --> 00:02:53.857
Your house is now part of the map, for any family in Southern California to find.

00:02:55.919 --> 00:02:57.925
Next up: Find lights near you.
